.TH PULSE 1 "October 2026" "Pulse-Active" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pulse \- minimalist real-time system monitor for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pulse
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pulse
shows CPU (usage, frequency and history graph), RAM, disk, network and
temperature information in real time. In a graphical session or any
UTF-8 terminal it draws the full coloured dashboard; on a Linux virtual
console it falls back to an ASCII layout.
.PP
Press any key to exit the interactive dashboard.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interval " " \fISECONDS\fR
Refresh interval in seconds (positive integer, default 1).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Single-line output instead of the dashboard. Selected automatically when
standard output is not a terminal.
.TP
.BR \-1 ", " \-\-once
Print one quiet-mode line and exit. Implies \fB\-\-quiet\fR.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-color
Disable colours (also disabled when \fBNO_COLOR\fR is set).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DISK_PATH
Mount point or directory whose disk usage is shown (default
.IR / ).
.TP
.B WM
Override window manager auto-detection.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set to a non-empty value, disable colours.
.SH QUIET OUTPUT
.EX
[12:00:00] CPU: 12%  RAM: 34%  DSK:  5%  NET D:0KB/s U:0KB/s  TEMP:45.0°C
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit.
.TP
.B 1
Missing essential commands or unusable
.IR /proc .
.TP
.B 2
Invalid option.
.SH OPTIONAL TOOLS
Temperatures are read from sysfs when available;
.BR sensors (1),
.BR nvidia\-smi (1),
.BR upower (1),
.BR xrandr (1)
and
.BR lspci (8)
add more detail when installed.
.SH AUTHOR
Carlos Corral <corral1976@gmail.com>
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR top (1),
.BR sensors (1)
